<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is an activated roller belt (ARB)?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A modular plastic belt with small embedded rollers that products ride on. When the rollers are driven from below, they move the product sideways or faster than the belt. When they are not driven, the product travels at belt speed. ARB handles diverting, sorting, singulation, alignment, merging, gapping, and turning without pusher arms or pop-up mechanisms above the conveying surface. It is Intralox's patented technology.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How does ARB technology work?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Rollers are set at a fixed angle to belt travel. Intralox Series 400 Angled Roller belts come at 0, 30, or 90 degrees, and custom belts can combine 0, 30, 45, and 60 degree rollers. An activation surface under the belt spins the rollers where product should move, pushing it along the roller direction while the belt carries it forward. Elsewhere the product travels at belt speed. Activation can be fixed or switched by the controls.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">ARB advantages over traditional diverters?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The moving parts that divert are below the conveying surface. Products are steered rather than struck. One belt can carry several functions and divert points. Fixed functions such as aligning and singulating work on touching or randomly spaced product, while selective sorting still needs enough space that only the target package is over an activated section. Confirm maintenance and gap requirements with the supplier.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What products can ARB handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Cases, cartons, trays, totes, polybags, mailers, and mixed parcels with a bottom that rests on and engages the rollers. Intralox notes behavior varies with shape, weight, conveyor design, and belt speed, so test unfamiliar products. Size limits depend on the equipment: Dorner rates its 3200 Series ARB conveyor for products as small as 6 by 6 inches at speeds up to 150 feet per minute.</p>

</div>
</div>
